                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> Don't Care 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> MC1 only 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> CCE1 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> TME on, PRMRR on/off 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> Don't Care 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> MC0+MC1 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> CCE0+CCE1 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> TME off, PRMRR on 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> Platform Features 
                  <sup class="+ topic/ph hi-d/sup "><b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b ">NOTE</b></sup> 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> MC0 or MC0+MC1 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> CCE0 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> TME off, PRMRR on 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry ">Platform Features 
                  <sup class="+ topic/ph hi-d/sup "><b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b ">NOTE</b></sup> 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> MC1 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> CCE1 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> TME off, PRMRR on 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> Zero 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> Any 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> None 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> TME off, PRMRR off 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> Don't Care 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> Any 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> None 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
            </tbody> 
          </tgroup> 
        </table> 
        <p class="- topic/p "> 
          <note id="GUID-F8B4A720-3D89-48F9-8351-0923FC5D0D92" class="- topic/note ">The PRMRR on/off is based upon platform features that utilizes PRMRR. In PTL, WCL, and WCL-R, when the KeyLocker or TDX feature is enabled, the BIOS will require the CCE enabled. 
            <ol id="GUID-A593B547-B1E3-45CB-8D7A-D50CDAE78549" class="- topic/ol "> 
              <li class="- topic/li ">BIOS shall program MEMSS_PMA_CR_BIOS_MEM_CONFIG BIT[5:4] in the Memory Subsystem PMA IP to enable CCE0/CCE1 IP out of reset. 
              </li> 
              <li class="- topic/li ">BIOS shall program MEMSS_PMA_CR_BIOS_MEM_CONFIG Bit[9] in the Memory Subsystem PMA IP to route all traffic to CCE. 
              </li> 
            </ol> 
          </note> 
        </p> 
      </li> 
      <li id="LI_0F06054BF39B470F8AC80E7CADE08904" class="- topic/li "> BIOS shall detect MKTME capability when MSR 981h IA32_TME_CAPABILITY[BIT2] =1 BIOS shall skip to step#14 below if MSR 981h IA32_TME_CAPABILITY[BIT2] = 0. 
      </li> 
      <li id="LI_DEDB4870FB214E3382A0BC7C571F6629" class="- topic/li "> BIOS shall detect max keys are not zero when MSR 981h IA32_TME_CAPABILITY[BIT50:36, BIT35:32] != 0. BIOS shall skip to step#14 below if MSR 981h IA32_TME_CAPABILITY[BIT50:36, BIT35:32] = 0. 
      </li> 
      <li id="LI_7BDB149E133147408A7D3E817992F531" class="- topic/li "> BIOS shall configure all of memory to be encrypted by programming MSR 983h IA32_​TME_​EXCLUDE_​MASK = 0 and MSR 984h IA32_​TME_​EXCLUDE_​BASE = 0. Excluding a memory range (keep a memory range unencrypted) is possible for special cases but not required. The single exclusion range applies to the KeyID=0 only. This specification does not define special cases for exclusion range usages. It is up to the designer to define special cases. 
        <note id="GUID-0A7876D5-D99E-48CF-8137-F0C8377B28AA" class="- topic/note "> The address range specified in this MSR must be the physical memory address under TOM (Top of Memory). 
        </note> 
      </li> 
      <li id="LI_04ADC48731074993A87F53431F1E2DE7" class="- topic/li "> BIOS shall determine TME Bypass support MSR 981h IA32_TME_CAPABILITY[BIT31] == 1. If supported than BIOS shall program MSR 982h IA32_TME_ACTIVATE[BIT31] based upon BIOS TME Bypass Policy. 
      </li> 
      <li id="LI_2836151BEE0048B1920430D43F470CBA" class="- topic/li "> BIOS shall detect TDX is enabled. BIOS shall split MK_TME_KEYID_BITS between MKTME and TDX KEY ID bits. The BIOS shall configure MSR 982h IA32_TME_ACTIVATE[39:16] = 1'b to allocate 7 Key ID bits for MKTME &amp; 8 Key ID bits for TDX keys for TDX as such: 
        <ul id="GUID-DFF78191-74A1-4050-9740-F6CEB143B489" class="- topic/ul "> 
          <li class="- topic/li ">MK_TME_MAX_KEYID_BITS is 4 therefore PA Address is Bit[45:42]. 
          </li> 
          <li class="- topic/li ">PA address bits[44:42] are for MKTME with KEY IDs. 
          </li> 
          <li class="- topic/li ">PA address bits[45:42] are for TDX with KEY IDs. 
          </li> 
        </ul> 
