      <li id="LI_A2034D22F4B74D309E3D3CA4E549B653" class="- topic/li "> BIOS shall program MSR 982h IA32_TME_ACTIVATE as one atomic operation because the MSR is Read-Write-Lock (RWL). 
      </li> 
      <li id="LI_5D14BB21A6BA41D3B5AF564D62607B43" class="- topic/li "> In Normal boot (S5/S4) the BIOS shall program MSR 982h IA32_TME_ACTIVATE as such: 
        <table id="GUID-DCCAA420-D63B-45AE-848B-4338122912AD" class="- topic/table "> 
          <tgroup cols="3" class="- topic/tgroup "> 
            <colspec colnum="1" colname="col1" colwidth="1.00*" class="- topic/colspec " /> 
            <colspec colnum="2" colname="col2" colwidth="1.50*" class="- topic/colspec " /> 
            <colspec colnum="3" colname="col3" colwidth="1.53*" class="- topic/colspec " /> 
            <thead class="- topic/thead "> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> IA32_TME_ACTIVATE MSR 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIOS Value 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> Description 
                </entry> 
              </row></thead> 
            <tbody class="- topic/tbody "> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIT[1] 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> 1'b 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> Enable TME 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIT[3:2] 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> 10'b 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> TME IP to generate new key 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIT[7:4] 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> 0010'b 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> AES-XTS-256 encryption algorithm to be used 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIT[31] 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> Any 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> *Based upon BIOS Policy 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIT[35:32] 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> MSR 982h IA32_TME_CAPABILITY [BIT35:32] 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> MAX Keys supported 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIT[39:16] 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> 1'b 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> *When TDX is enabled in BIOS. Otherwise default 0'b. 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIT[50] 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> 1'b 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> AES-XTS-256 encryption algorithm to be used 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
            </tbody> 
          </tgroup> 
        </table> 
      </li> 
      <li id="LI_B46C7906FC604EF09A235446BB082ACF" class="- topic/li "> In Warm Reset, S3 Resume, Capsule Update, where memory is preserved, the BIOS shall program MSR 982h IA32_TME_ACTIVATE as such: 
        <table id="GUID-613FE33A-F0CF-4193-AB2A-E19E6EF3294B" class="- topic/table "> 
          <tgroup cols="3" class="- topic/tgroup "> 
            <colspec colnum="1" colname="col1" colwidth="1.00*" class="- topic/colspec " /> 
            <colspec colnum="2" colname="col2" colwidth="1.42*" class="- topic/colspec " /> 
            <colspec colnum="3" colname="col3" colwidth="1.46*" class="- topic/colspec " /> 
            <thead class="- topic/thead "> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> IA32_TME_ACTIVATE MSR 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIOS Value 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> Description 
                </entry> 
              </row></thead> 
            <tbody class="- topic/tbody "> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIT[1] 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> 1'b 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> Enable TME 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIT[3:2] 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> 01'b 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> TME IP to generate new key 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIT[7:4] 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> 0010'b 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> AES-XTS-256 encryption algorithm to be used 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIT[31] 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> Any 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> *Based upon BIOS Policy 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIT[35:32] 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> MSR 982h IA32_TME_CAPABILITY [BIT35:32] 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> MAX Keys supported 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIT[39:16] 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> 1'b 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> *When TDX is enabled in BIOS. Otherwise default 0'b. 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
              <row class="- topic/row "> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIT[50] 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> 1'b 
                </entry> 
                <entry class="- topic/entry "> AES-XTS-256 encryption algorithm to be used 
                </entry> 
              </row> 
            </tbody> 
          </tgroup> 
        </table> 
      </li> 
      <li id="LI_B0C55235E44C4CD79115903917F43DD4" class="- topic/li "> BIOS shall program all zeroes to MK_TME_CORE_ACTIVATE (0x9FF) MSR register on each CPU Core. 
      </li> 
      <li id="LI_ADAA225EBC1E4E919F9FB3E9E6AE6D51" class="- topic/li "> BIOS shall program two CCE_CONTROL_0_0_0_MCHBAR registers in the CCE IP with same values as MEMORY_SLICE_HASH register in the HBO IP. 
      </li> 
      <li class="- topic/li "> BIOS shall program two REMAP_BASE and REMAP_LIMIT registers in the CCE IP with same values as REMAP_BASE &amp; REMAP_LIMIT registers in the HBO IP. 
      </li> 
      <li class="- topic/li "> BIOS shall disable MKTME if the MSR indicate no support in steps# 4 above. 
        <ol id="GUID-0D71E83B-FE2F-4DE9-9092-FD9C1120C71C" class="- topic/ol "> 
          <li class="- topic/li ">MSR 982h IA32_TME_ACTIVATE[BIT1] = 0 
          </li> 
        </ol> 
      </li> 
      <li class="- topic/li "> BIOS shall complete MRC_DONE. This step is done outside of MKTME initialization. 
      </li> 
      <li class="- topic/li "> BIOS shall hard code BIOS_MAX_PA to 42. BIOS will not allocate MMIO above 41 bits. 
      </li> 
    </ol> 
    <note id="GUID-58E14D98-C582-4BFA-98C9-E755702A62A8" class="- topic/note "> 
      <ul id="UL_EE17653F9B3B40B596EEB3306AF0981B" class="- topic/ul "> 
        <li id="LI_8A06CF5B932547909354A629C2CB50C0" class="- topic/li "> TME key#0 is hardware managed that is no accessible to the software. 
        </li> 
        <li id="LI_45E06724C0A94CBEA28B729A938C9E03" class="- topic/li "> For Multiple keys related use case, software needs to provide the keys. These keys can be key#1 onwards. 
        </li> 
